!**/*.meta
src/Tests~/**/*.meta

## Unity-generated .meta for the source this branch exposes to a Unity project.
## This repository is consumed as a git submodule under a Unity project's Assets/, so Unity
## generates a .meta next to every file it imports. Those belong to the consuming project, not
## here — committing them would make every `git pull` in the submodule conflict with whatever
## the local Unity happened to generate.
##
## Consequence to know about: the guids are NOT stable across clones. Any .asmdef in the
## consuming project that references these assemblies must reference them BY NAME, never by
## "GUID:...", or the reference silently breaks on a fresh clone.
src/ECS/**/*.meta
src/Klotho/**/*.meta

## One exception, and it has to be one: KlothoGenerator.dll is a Roslyn source generator, and the
## ONLY place Unity records "run this as a generator" is the RoslynAnalyzer label inside its .meta.
## Without this file committed, a fresh clone imports the DLL as an inert plugin, the generator
## never runs, and every [KlothoSerializable] type fails to compile with "does not implement
## inherited abstract member" — ~550 errors that look nothing like the actual cause.
## Its guid is fixed here rather than left to Unity so it stays stable across clones.
!src/Klotho/Analyzers/KlothoGenerator.dll.meta

*.DotSettings.user

